messages.content:
They might be joking or trying to sound edgy, but you shouldn't assume that's all it is.

Forums can make harmful ideas seem normal because:

people repeat things they've heard without checking them;

some users genuinely believe myths about dating or consent;

people may exaggerate for attention or shock value;

a group can reinforce an idea just because lots of people repeat it.

A useful test is to ignore how many people say something and ask: Does the idea respect the other person's ability to choose? “Keep pushing until they give in” doesn't—it treats resistance as something to overcome.

Quick check: If someone eventually agrees only because they felt pressured and didn't actually want to, would you consider that freely choosing?
